abstract: >-
  A technical note on an elementary sign-averaging inequality for lattice gauge theories with a central involution, and its formalisation in Lean 4 (23 declarations).
  Multiplying by -1 all links of a column and averaging over independent column signs gives |<W>| <= tanh(kappa)^|A| (abstract form), an elementary area law
  tanh(beta|F|)^area on (plate) x (finite fibre), and, on a periodic base torus, a twist-ratio bound |Z_0 - Z_1| <= tanh(kappa)^N (Z_0 + Z_1). The head theorem is stated
  and proved in Lean on the lattice, the energy and the SU(2) of OpenAI's public Lean development: for every period l >= 2 and beta >= 0,
  |Z_0 - Z_1| <= tanh(beta l^2)^(l^2) (Z_0 + Z_1), where Z_1 has the sign of the plaquettes of one base point of the (0,1)-plane reversed. The bound is elementary and valid at
  every coupling, but degenerates as the transverse section grows at fixed beta; it says nothing about the mass gap in dimension four or about weak coupling. The centre-multiplication
  tool is classical (Tomboulis-Yaffe 1985, Appendix I.C; Kovacs-Tomboulis 2002, eq. (8)) and the twist ratio is the classical quantity of 't Hooft; no priority is claimed. Version 1.2 (12 November 2026): adds a section on a cyclic centre Z_N (16 further Lean declarations; Fourier bound |sum_k zeta^{qk} Z_k| <= rho^{|P|} sum_k Z_k with rho = 1 - exp(-2 kappa), N = 2 of the published statements derived from it; SU(N) on the 4D lattice and the improvement rho <= tanh(kappa) on paper only). Version 1.1: literature corrections only. A paper-only derivation (not in Lean, checked by AI models only) gives lambda_1/lambda_0 <= tanh(beta L^2)^l for the
  centre-parity sectors of a tube transfer matrix. Not refereed; no human has checked the proofs.
